  "rationale": "Adds workflow-level concurrency with cancel-in-progress scoped to the same workflow and branch (P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE). When a new push to master arrives while a build+CTS matrix run is still in progress, the older run is cancelled because the newer revision supersedes it, saving VM time on redundant builds. All matrix configurations and the conformance test suite are still executed for the latest commit, so build and test coverage is preserved. Prerequisites are met: a single workflow on one branch where newer revisions supersede older ones; no release/deployment work; the group key includes github.ref so branches are isolated (only master is triggered anyway). No permissions are weakened, no new actions/secrets/network/deployment operations are added.",
